cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If ttl3d helped your work, please cite it as below."
title: "ttl3d: a self-contained 3D and 2D HTML viewer for RDF graphs"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Abadifard
    given-names: Soheil
version: 0.2.2
date-released: 2026-09-11
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/soheilabadifard/TTL_to_3D"
url: "https://soheilabadifard.github.io/TTL_to_3D/"
abstract: >-
  ttl3d turns one or more RDF files (Turtle, N-Triples, RDF/XML, JSON-LD) into a
  single self-contained HTML page that shows the graph in 3D or 2D, with labels,
  a legend by file, type or namespace, label search and a detail card for every
  node. The page embeds all of its JavaScript, so it opens from a file and works
  offline.
keywords:
  - RDF
  - Turtle
  - OWL
  - ontology
  - knowledge graph
  - semantic web
  - linked data
  - graph visualization
